---
/**
 * Not found.
 *
 * wrangler.jsonc sets not_found_handling to "404-page", which makes Cloudflare
 * serve /404.html for an unmatched path. There was no such file, so an unmatched
 * path returned a 404 with an empty body and the reader got a blank page with no
 * way back. Astro emits this route as dist/404.html in a static build, which is
 * exactly the file that setting is looking for.
 *
 * No search box, because a search box needs JavaScript or a backend and the site
 * has neither. The nav is the way back, and it is already in the layout.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Not found"
  description="That page does not exist on this site."
  cites={[]}
>
  <section class="section section--open">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="masthead">
        <h1>Not found</h1>
        <p class="masthead__meta mono">404</p>
      </div>

      <div class="doc">
        <p class="lede">
          There is no page at that address. Either it never existed, or it moved and something
          still points at where it used to be.
        </p>

        <p>
          Internal links are checked when the site is built. A broken internal link can be
          reported on the <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Where to go instead</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/">The dashboard</a>, which has the headline figure from every section.</li>
          <li><a href="/progress/">Progress</a> for what models can do, and <a href="/capability/">Capability</a> for what it took to build them.</li>
          <li><a href="/policy/">Policy</a> for the law that applies, by jurisdiction.</li>
          <li><a href="/sources/">Sources</a> for every dataset behind the numbers, with its licence.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
